  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Idaho has $155M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Federal buying in Idaho shows a sharp pullback compared with prior years: obligations are down 96.4% year over year. Idaho has 288 awards so far, with an average award size of $537K. Year-to-year history shows a peak and decline pattern: FY22 had $2.5B, FY23 had $3.2B, FY24 had $3.8B, FY25 had $4B, FY26 had $4.3B, and FY27 has $155M. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in the state with $177M in obligations. BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC is the largest vendor with $90.5M, followed by IDAHO ENVIRONMENTAL COALITION LLC with $83.2M. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services and Remediation Services are the top industries with $90.5M and $83.2M respectively. These totals reflect FY2027 to date activity and the current-year numbers are partial for the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations are down 96.4% year over year. Idaho has $155M in FY2027 to date compared with $4.3B in FY26 and earlier yearly totals. Award activity shows 288 awards so far, and the average award size is $537K. The sharp decline concentrates federal spending into a much smaller current-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the primary buyers and vendors in Idaho now?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the top buying agency with $177M. BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC leads vendors with $90.5M and IDAHO ENVIRONMENTAL COALITION LLC follows with $83.2M. The largest industries are All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $90.5M and Remediation Services at $83.2M."
      }
    ]
